# KnowledgeOS - Database Design

# Part 7 - Chat Messages

---

# 21. Table — Chat Messages

---

# 21.1 Purpose

The `chat_messages` table stores every message exchanged between the user and the KnowledgeOS AI assistant.

Unlike `chat_sessions`, which stores conversation-level metadata, this table stores the actual conversational content.

Each row represents one immutable message generated by either:

- User
- Assistant
- System (future)

The table also stores retrieval metadata, generation statistics, citations, and agent execution information, making it the primary audit trail for every AI interaction.

---

# 21.2 Relationships

```text
profiles

│

└──────────── chat_sessions

                    │

                    │ 1 : N

                    ▼

              chat_messages
```

Each chat session contains multiple chat messages.

Each message belongs to exactly one chat session.

Messages cannot exist independently.

---

# 21.3 Message Lifecycle

```text
User Prompt

↓

Message Saved

↓

Planner Agent

↓

Retriever

↓

Prompt Builder

↓

LLM

↓

Reviewer Agent

↓

Assistant Response

↓

Message Saved

↓

Conversation Updated
```

Every interaction produces at least:

- One User Message
- One Assistant Message

Future versions may also include System Messages.

