# 21.10 Retrieval Metadata

Unlike traditional chat applications, KnowledgeOS stores retrieval metadata alongside AI responses.

Each assistant message may contain:

- Retrieved document IDs
- Retrieved chunk IDs
- Source citations
- Token statistics
- AI model information
- Response latency

This enables complete explainability for every generated response.

Example:

```text
Assistant Response

↓

Retrieved:

• Operating Systems.pdf

• DBMS Notes.pdf

↓

Chunks:

18

24

31
```

---

# 21.11 Citation Storage

Source references are stored separately from the natural language response.

Example

```json
{
  "documents": [
    "Operating Systems.pdf",
    "DBMS Notes.pdf"
  ],
  "chunks": [
    "chunk-18",
    "chunk-24",
    "chunk-31"
  ]
}
```

Keeping citations structured allows the frontend to:

- Display clickable citations
- Open source documents
- Highlight referenced passages
- Support future citation exports

without parsing generated text.

